WEBVTT

00:00.025 --> 00:30.029
Crib in the Locker

00:00.533 --> 00:02.206
A lullaby by a delinquent girl.

00:02.353 --> 00:05.713
It's the sorrowful ballad of
a small abandoned life

00:05.920 --> 00:07.306
and the girl who saves it.

00:08.727 --> 00:09.134
Are you...

00:09.159 --> 00:09.994
Shut the hell up!

00:10.380 --> 00:14.068
Neither Daddy nor Mom care about me.

00:15.371 --> 00:16.498
Damn it!

00:16.705 --> 00:18.178
He's suffering from severe malnutrition.

00:18.485 --> 00:19.212
Please save him!

00:19.411 --> 00:20.605
Why are you so desperate to save him?

00:20.651 --> 00:23.544
Someday I'm going to leave home
and live alone with him.

00:23.705 --> 00:25.932
Ohmibaby!

00:26.111 --> 00:29.531
Black Jack, Today's Karte - Crib in the Locker.

00:30.035 --> 00:36.658
I'm going to fly to where you are.

00:30.035 --> 00:36.658
kimi no moto e tonde yuku yo

00:36.993 --> 00:43.999
I know I can spread my wings when I want to see you.

00:36.993 --> 00:43.999
aitai toki tsubasa hiraku

00:44.584 --> 00:47.669
Nobody knows

00:44.584 --> 00:47.669
dara nimo wakaranai

00:48.088 --> 00:51.507
when a miracle might occur,

00:48.088 --> 00:51.507
kiseki wa itsu okiru?

00:51.508 --> 00:57.930
but it feels like my wish is finally coming true.

00:51.508 --> 00:57.930
nozomi wa kanaeraresou de

00:57.931 --> 01:04.728
Because there's only one place I want to go,

00:57.931 --> 01:04.728
mukau basho wa hitotsu shika nai kara

01:04.729 --> 01:07.981
iro asenai omoi yosete

01:04.729 --> 01:07.981
I gather my feelings whose colors never fade,

01:07.982 --> 01:11.527
and now it seems I'm dreaming.

01:07.982 --> 01:11.527
saa Dreaming now

01:12.112 --> 01:15.447
I'm living for your sake?

01:12.112 --> 01:15.447
kimi no tame ni iketeru

01:15.448 --> 01:18.617
I will be your strength,

01:15.448 --> 01:18.617
donna chikara nimo naru

01:18.910 --> 01:21.829
no matter how far apart we are.

01:18.910 --> 01:21.829
Far away Far away harukana

01:21.830 --> 01:25.624
So Freedom. So Freedom.

01:25.750 --> 01:29.211
I will send you

01:25.750 --> 01:29.211
kimi no tame no okurou

01:29.212 --> 01:32.464
the beautiful blossom of this flower.

01:29.212 --> 01:32.464
kirei ni saita hana wo

01:32.632 --> 01:35.551
So let's look for shooting stars.

01:32.632 --> 01:35.551
Shooting Star Shooting Star sagasou

01:35.552 --> 01:39.555
So Freedom. So Freedom.

02:17.830 --> 02:20.997
Originally "Baby Blues" by Tezuka Osamu

02:17.830 --> 02:20.997
Crib in the Locker

02:24.519 --> 02:26.311
Pinoco-chan, can you pass that?

02:26.312 --> 02:27.229
Sure.

02:29.649 --> 02:31.900
Put this at the very top.

02:31.901 --> 02:32.901
OK.

02:34.904 --> 02:37.281
It's all ready now!

02:37.282 --> 02:38.626
Are you ready for this?

02:44.914 --> 02:46.290
It's pretty.

02:47.000 --> 02:49.168
The tree's done now.

02:53.506 --> 02:55.257
This is for helping us.

02:56.764 --> 02:58.260
This looks yummy!

02:59.304 --> 03:00.929
I was just getting hungry!

03:01.044 --> 03:02.764
Thank you!

03:03.683 --> 03:07.186
Anyway, I need to get ready to open the shop.

03:08.313 --> 03:11.815
Wato-san, would you come shopping with me later?

03:11.816 --> 03:15.152
I want to go buy a Christmas present for Master.

03:15.153 --> 03:17.112
Sure, I want to go shopping too.

03:17.255 --> 03:19.740
Onee-chan, I want action figures.

03:19.741 --> 03:20.949
I didn't ask you.

03:22.452 --> 03:25.954
Come on, I'm protecting our home while Dad's away!

03:25.955 --> 03:27.706
Please?

03:27.707 --> 03:30.250
Christmas presents, huh...

03:38.426 --> 03:40.802
That's so cute!

03:41.846 --> 03:43.138
I'll take this.

03:43.139 --> 03:45.562
And please wrap it as a gift.

03:45.850 --> 03:46.892
OK.

03:49.520 --> 03:52.731
I'm sure Doc will be happy with this.

03:52.732 --> 03:55.150
Then that teacher...

03:56.110 --> 03:59.196
He said he'll expel me if I cause trouble again.

04:00.740 --> 04:02.032
Let's show him a thing or two.

04:05.536 --> 04:07.412
Ohmigewdness!

04:07.413 --> 04:09.289
Where do ya wanna go now?

04:09.582 --> 04:10.999
Hey! Apologize to me!

04:13.211 --> 04:15.671
You broke the mug!

04:15.767 --> 04:16.441
Move.

04:16.615 --> 04:17.965
Apologize!

04:18.118 --> 04:21.593
You better move, or we'll hurt you.

04:21.617 --> 04:22.448
Stop it.

04:22.679 --> 04:24.882
Why bother acting tough against a kid?

04:28.238 --> 04:29.559
I'm not a kid!

04:29.560 --> 04:31.645
I'm eighteen years old!

04:31.646 --> 04:35.482
I'm much more grown up than you!

04:36.567 --> 04:37.553
Grown up?

04:38.027 --> 04:41.363
Then you'll pay for this.

04:52.546 --> 04:53.746
Where's Pinoco?

04:56.629 --> 04:57.879
Doc...

04:58.423 --> 05:00.173
Please release her.

05:00.407 --> 05:02.469
I can't let her go for free.

05:02.802 --> 05:04.678
What did she do?

05:05.221 --> 05:08.307
She tripped on her own, then tried to blame it on us.

05:08.308 --> 05:09.891
Th-That's not true!

05:09.892 --> 05:11.810
She was swinging around her bag and—

05:11.811 --> 05:13.186
That's enough.

05:13.187 --> 05:14.771
Pinoco, let's go.

05:15.038 --> 05:17.190
Hey, are you trying to run from us?

05:17.608 --> 05:18.723
Here's my address.

05:18.985 --> 05:20.450
Come to my place if you want to talk.

05:23.156 --> 05:24.740
Let her go.

05:24.741 --> 05:26.742
Doc.

05:26.743 --> 05:27.799
Let's go.

05:30.538 --> 05:33.539
Maggie! Why'd you let them leave?!

05:33.791 --> 05:38.170
He's Black Jack, a doctor with a shady business.

05:38.671 --> 05:40.166
There's no need to rush.

05:40.381 --> 05:42.804
I'll milk him for all he's worth.

05:45.636 --> 05:47.147
Stop crying already.

05:47.555 --> 05:49.264
But I'm so frustrated.

05:49.265 --> 05:52.174
I'll show them next time!

05:52.643 --> 05:54.728
By the way, what's in that box?

05:56.064 --> 05:57.506
It's nothing.

06:02.320 --> 06:06.031
I heard he makes big money.

06:06.032 --> 06:09.910
So we won't have to worry about money if we scare him.

06:09.911 --> 06:11.203
Maggie.

06:11.204 --> 06:13.372
Maggie, look.

06:13.373 --> 06:14.373
What's that?

06:14.374 --> 06:15.874
It's a key for a locker.

06:16.376 --> 06:18.919
I took it from some twenty year old woman.

06:18.920 --> 06:20.003
Idiot.

06:20.004 --> 06:21.382
Why take something like that?

06:21.881 --> 06:25.967
What if we go there and the police are waiting?

06:25.968 --> 06:27.260
Don't worry.

06:27.261 --> 06:31.098
I scared her good.

06:33.559 --> 06:35.977
Don't worry, there's nobody.

06:37.730 --> 06:41.691
Whatever's in there won't be worth much,
if she's willing to put it in a locker.

06:41.692 --> 06:43.360
Let's check it out.

06:50.403 --> 06:51.743
What the hell's this?!

06:52.022 --> 06:53.714
Is it dead?

06:53.996 --> 06:55.907
It's still breathing.

06:56.374 --> 06:58.625
This is useless!

07:00.461 --> 07:01.837
What do we do?!

07:01.838 --> 07:03.088
I don't know!

07:03.464 --> 07:04.381
Let's leave.

07:04.382 --> 07:05.507
We'll be in trouble if we stay.

07:06.384 --> 07:08.718
Let's go clubbing for a change.

07:23.359 --> 07:26.736
Hey, I wonder what happened to that baby?

07:26.737 --> 07:28.690
Maybe it died already.

07:28.948 --> 07:30.787
Stop talking about the baby!

07:32.352 --> 07:35.302
Who cares if it lives or dies?

07:35.580 --> 07:37.707
That baby's been abandoned by its parents anyway.

08:01.939 --> 08:04.524
Welcome home, young lady.

08:04.764 --> 08:05.984
Where's Mom and Dad?

08:05.985 --> 08:10.113
Master is on the road for a conference,
and won't be back tonight.

08:10.114 --> 08:14.409
Mistress is on a live show on TV.
She won't be heme until midnight.

08:14.647 --> 08:15.785
Would you like dinner?

08:15.786 --> 08:16.964
I don't want any.

08:19.373 --> 08:20.916
This is delicious!

08:20.917 --> 08:25.921
Your daughter is so lucky that she
gets to eat this all the time.

08:25.922 --> 08:28.548
I hope everyone will try this at home to—

08:28.847 --> 08:32.594
I haven't eaten your cooking in years.

08:34.555 --> 08:38.099
<i>Neither Daddy nor Mom care about me.</i>

08:46.192 --> 08:47.359
<i>Does he...</i>

08:57.370 --> 08:58.286
<i>Damn it!</i>

09:15.638 --> 09:16.764
He's alive.

09:28.693 --> 09:30.944
What is it, Largo?

09:32.029 --> 09:33.947
Who could it be, so late at night?

09:37.955 --> 09:39.244
I-It's you!

09:39.467 --> 09:41.652
You broke my mug!

09:46.460 --> 09:50.463
Doc, the girl from earlier is here.

09:50.464 --> 09:51.715
Let her in.

09:53.217 --> 09:54.968
So, how much do you want?

09:54.969 --> 09:56.015
Doc.

10:01.726 --> 10:03.268
What's with the baby?

10:03.728 --> 10:05.972
The baby's dying.

10:06.314 --> 10:08.014
You can save him, can't you?

10:11.356 --> 10:13.176
He's suffering from severe malnutrition.

10:13.696 --> 10:16.708
He wasn't given food right after his birth.

10:17.158 --> 10:20.201
And his leg bones and vertebrae are crooked from Rickets.

10:20.369 --> 10:21.465
Please save him!

10:21.829 --> 10:24.372
Then I won't ask for anything else!

10:24.373 --> 10:25.741
I refuse.

10:26.500 --> 10:29.183
I don't have the facilities to take care of a baby.

10:29.594 --> 10:31.838
Take him to another hospital if you're worried.

10:31.839 --> 10:33.613
But you're unlicensed!

10:34.050 --> 10:37.041
I'll report to you police if you don't do this!

10:37.261 --> 10:38.310
I don't care.

10:38.863 --> 10:39.863
Go ahead.

10:41.557 --> 10:43.377
You can't threaten me.

10:43.726 --> 10:45.001
Take him away.

10:54.602 --> 10:56.120
Doc...

11:09.251 --> 11:12.099
Poor baby, you're so dirty.

11:12.336 --> 11:13.983
Let me change you quickly.

11:28.261 --> 11:30.464
I'll come back again late tomorrow.

11:31.148 --> 11:32.107
Good night.

11:46.497 --> 11:47.914
You followed me?

11:47.915 --> 11:48.957
Damn it!

11:48.958 --> 11:51.167
He's been abandoned!

11:51.251 --> 11:52.062
I'm not lying!

11:52.464 --> 11:54.272
I didn't accuse you of lying.

11:54.797 --> 11:57.757
Why are you taking care of him?

11:58.102 --> 12:00.093
He'll starve to death if I don't!

12:00.511 --> 12:02.595
Then report him to the station office.

12:02.596 --> 12:05.014
But then they'll find out about our theft.

12:05.015 --> 12:06.215
I see.

12:06.600 --> 12:10.278
You want to save the baby,
but you don't want to admit your theft, huh?

12:11.147 --> 12:13.815
But the baby will die at this rate.

12:20.906 --> 12:22.031
Please!

12:22.032 --> 12:23.570
Please save the baby!

12:23.784 --> 12:25.379
I'll do whatever you ask of me.

12:25.995 --> 12:28.538
Please save him...

12:29.206 --> 12:30.582
Please!

12:33.335 --> 12:36.481
I will operate on him, but that alone won't make him well.

12:37.590 --> 12:43.175
You have to keep giving him milk enriched with calcium,
vitamin D, and phosphorus compounds.

12:44.555 --> 12:46.514
I'll take care of him.

12:47.016 --> 12:48.725
Why are you so desperate to save him?

12:53.213 --> 12:53.831
Well, whatever.

12:54.023 --> 12:56.472
We can keep him until his bandages come off.

12:56.734 --> 12:58.215
I won't have anything to do with him after that,

12:58.527 --> 13:00.667
Yeah, fine.

13:03.157 --> 13:05.450
Good morning, Doc.

13:11.791 --> 13:14.292
Ohmibaby!

13:17.668 --> 13:19.099
I see.

13:19.548 --> 13:21.633
But what do we do now?

13:22.343 --> 13:25.303
My part of the promise is to treat the baby.

13:25.304 --> 13:26.596
But...

13:27.264 --> 13:29.140
Oh my, what should I do?

13:29.141 --> 13:30.600
Well... um...

13:30.601 --> 13:32.264
Does he need a new diaper?

13:32.478 --> 13:34.562
I just changed it.

13:39.652 --> 13:41.361
Shut up!

13:51.497 --> 13:54.520
I've had enough of babysitting for a while.

13:58.219 --> 14:02.298
But why is he quiet when you're holding him?

14:02.663 --> 14:05.385
Maybe he thinks you're his mother.

14:10.975 --> 14:12.278
Thank you, Doctor.

14:12.893 --> 14:13.977
And you too.

14:14.937 --> 14:16.465
I'll come again tomorrow night.

14:17.940 --> 14:19.638
Thank goodness.

14:32.246 --> 14:35.373
She was totally a wuss.

14:36.125 --> 14:37.584
M-Maggie!

14:39.587 --> 14:40.398
What?

14:41.130 --> 14:43.673
You haven't been hanging out with us.

14:44.087 --> 14:45.475
I've been busy.

14:45.968 --> 14:48.269
We're going to the usual club.

14:48.512 --> 14:49.668
Wanna come?

14:50.306 --> 14:51.723
I don't feel like it.

14:52.839 --> 14:54.572
What about that doctor?

14:54.977 --> 14:57.270
You said he'd be a good source of money.

14:57.606 --> 14:59.331
H-He was no good.

14:59.690 --> 15:01.441
It was really tough to get him.

15:01.859 --> 15:05.594
Then let's raid his house now.

15:07.239 --> 15:08.364
What was that for?!

15:08.824 --> 15:11.034
I'm getting out of this group!

15:11.035 --> 15:12.201
What?!

15:12.202 --> 15:14.621
Do you know what happens to a traitor?

15:20.252 --> 15:21.419
Get her!

15:39.813 --> 15:41.272
What happened to you?!

15:46.779 --> 15:48.446
Tell, me what happened.

15:49.323 --> 15:53.284
Don't act like a mom just because
you happen to be home early!

16:01.193 --> 16:04.504
<i>I still have him.</i>

16:24.775 --> 16:29.487
It's not easy taking care of him, but he's so cute.

16:32.032 --> 16:36.296
Are you still sneaking out of house every
night to take care of the baby?

16:36.704 --> 16:37.649
Yeah.

16:38.747 --> 16:40.957
Why don't you report him already?

16:41.333 --> 16:42.458
No way!

16:44.962 --> 16:48.965
Someday I'm going to leave home and live alone with him.

16:51.468 --> 16:52.768
Doctor, here.

16:54.138 --> 16:56.014
It's payment for all the appointments and treatment.

16:56.303 --> 16:58.640
Where did you get so much money

16:59.199 --> 17:01.352
I borrowed it from the safe at home.

17:01.729 --> 17:05.189
Keep it, since you did so much for us.

17:06.693 --> 17:08.321
I don't want any stolen money.

17:08.652 --> 17:09.569
Take it home.

17:28.201 --> 17:30.048
Where do you sneak off to every night?

17:32.342 --> 17:34.107
Are you with those delinquent friends of yours?

17:34.595 --> 17:37.638
No, I broke up with them.

17:38.223 --> 17:39.640
Then why can't you tell us?

17:41.514 --> 17:44.079
Maggie! What's that money?!

17:45.189 --> 17:46.814
I borrowed it from the safe.

17:47.191 --> 17:48.566
How could you?!

17:48.567 --> 17:49.741
Shut the hell up!

17:49.985 --> 17:52.437
What do you know about me, huh?!

17:52.780 --> 17:54.363
Do you have any right to preach to me?!

17:54.364 --> 17:56.616
Why you!

17:56.695 --> 17:57.218
What are you doing?

17:57.242 --> 17:58.517
Come!

18:00.458 --> 18:03.972
I won't allow you out of this room
until you learn to behave!

18:05.667 --> 18:07.608
Let me out! Let me out!

18:07.961 --> 18:09.337
Let me out of here!

18:10.005 --> 18:11.178
Let me out!

18:14.918 --> 18:15.752
What now?

18:16.220 --> 18:18.375
Without me, the baby will...

18:35.280 --> 18:36.217
Baby.

18:41.370 --> 18:43.329
Damn! Damn it!

18:49.670 --> 18:51.796
<i>My baby...</i>

19:35.632 --> 19:36.708
Baby...

19:43.270 --> 19:45.276
<i>Maybe he died.</i>

19:45.893 --> 19:49.450
<i>The station staff must have found
him and taken him away.</i>

20:00.199 --> 20:04.239
It's about the baby found and rescued
from inside a coin locker.

20:04.661 --> 20:08.753
What is strange is that there are signs that
the baby was being raised in the locker.

20:09.708 --> 20:11.876
There are signs of surgery and shots as well.

20:09.709 --> 20:10.918
How did you—

20:11.877 --> 20:15.024
The baby is thought to have survived because of them.

20:16.256 --> 20:19.467
The baby was taken by Child Protective Services.

20:19.468 --> 20:24.847
However, the police are searching for the parents
of this miracle baby found on Christmas Eve.

20:47.996 --> 20:51.432
So you called the station?

20:51.708 --> 20:54.293
I thought it was strange that you didn't come.

20:56.213 --> 20:57.838
Thank you, Doctor.

20:58.465 --> 21:02.079
I'll go see the baby once things are settled on my end.

21:06.056 --> 21:07.901
Merry Christmas!

21:09.518 --> 21:10.851
We're all here now.

21:11.478 --> 21:13.020
Here's the cake, Master.

21:13.563 --> 21:15.314
All right, let's get started.

21:17.609 --> 21:19.819
I'll get going now.

21:19.820 --> 21:22.363
We're having a Christmas party now.

21:22.364 --> 21:23.906
Would you care to join us?

21:24.102 --> 21:26.472
Thank you, but I'll go.

21:26.827 --> 21:31.914
For some reason, my mother said she’ll
be waiting at home with a cake.

21:31.915 --> 21:33.666
Really?

21:34.084 --> 21:35.957
This one's for you.

21:40.507 --> 21:41.904
Hey, that's...

21:42.175 --> 21:44.405
It's what I broke.

21:44.845 --> 21:46.220
A Unico mug.

21:47.055 --> 21:49.015
You remembered.

21:59.026 --> 22:01.598
Merry Christmas, Doc.

22:05.240 --> 22:06.240
Thank you.

22:07.576 --> 22:10.244
Merry Christmas!

22:24.096 --> 22:29.208
As you look at the ground uncertainly,

22:24.096 --> 22:29.208
tamerai gachi no fuseta hitomi

22:29.209 --> 22:34.505
I gently pull your hair closer to me.

22:29.209 --> 22:34.505
kono te ga sono kami hikiyoseteta

22:35.136 --> 22:41.637
You didn't speak, but only sighed,

22:35.136 --> 22:41.637
nani mo iezu ni kobore ochita tameiki

22:41.638 --> 22:46.100
and wet my chest with your tears.

22:41.638 --> 22:46.100
namida ga mune wo nurashita

22:46.101 --> 22:51.355
You longed to hear it, even if it was a lie.

22:46.101 --> 22:51.355
use demo ii... to kitto nozonde ita

22:51.356 --> 22:56.110
But I couldn't give you the answer you wanted.

22:51.356 --> 22:56.110
kimi no kimochi ni kotae kirezu

22:56.111 --> 23:04.535
If I gave you that answer, despite my cowardice,

22:56.111 --> 23:04.535
okubyou na boku ga moshi sono toki kotaetetara mada

23:04.536 --> 23:08.122
would we still be together?

23:04.536 --> 23:08.122
tsuzuiteita noka?

23:08.123 --> 23:13.419
That irregular breath my body was accustomed to,

23:08.123 --> 23:13.419
karada ga oboeta fukisoku na breath

23:13.423 --> 23:18.883
I want to feel it one more time.

23:13.423 --> 23:18.883
mou ichido subete de kanjitai

23:18.884 --> 23:24.388
The breath of surprise when I lost everything.

23:18.884 --> 23:24.388
subete wo nakushita fuyoui na breath

23:24.389 --> 23:33.564
And the pain that binds me every time I feel regret.

23:24.389 --> 23:33.564
kuyamu tabi mata sono itami ga shimetsukeru

23:45.053 --> 24:15.082
Fortunes & Misfortunes of a False Mother & Son

23:46.273 --> 23:48.273
The love and sorrow of a
false mother and son.

23:49.260 --> 23:54.331
I finally have the ideal family I've always wanted.

23:54.840 --> 23:56.633
A man pretending to be another woman's son

23:56.673 --> 23:59.546
feels more loved by his false mother
than by his real family.

24:00.053 --> 24:02.206
Give me a facelift; into this face.

24:02.373 --> 24:04.133
You can look like anyone you want.

24:04.227 --> 24:05.376
Please stop!

24:05.529 --> 24:07.825
Were things going well with that mother?

24:07.949 --> 24:09.669
There's something I must tell you.

24:10.003 --> 24:10.796
